# PART 8 — AI/ML EVALUATION INTEGRITY

This section is mandatory.

The reported 90.91% accuracy on 22 records must not automatically be treated as a production-valid metric.

Implement a proper evaluation pipeline:

1. Identify labelled training data.
2. Validate labels.
3. Separate training and testing records.
4. Prevent data leakage.
5. Use stratified splitting where appropriate.
6. Use cross-validation when dataset size permits.
7. Calculate accuracy.
8. Calculate macro precision.
9. Calculate macro recall.
10. Calculate macro F1.
11. Calculate per-class metrics.
12. Generate a confusion matrix.
13. Record evaluation sample size.
14. Record model version.
15. Record evaluation date.
16. Measure inference latency using a documented method.

If the dataset is too small:
- Display insufficient evaluation data.
- Show sample size.
- Report limitations.
- Do not label the model production-validated.

Keep training and evaluation data separate.

Do not use training-set accuracy as test accuracy.

Do not claim that a heuristic algorithm is a trained ML model.

